va</em> 'Marvel of Four Seasons'","entityDescription":"A heritage variety from 1885, this red and green butterhead lettuce is very attractive, with beautiful crumpled deep red leaves and an open structure around a small heart. It has an excellent flavour and can be harvested as baby leaves as needed or as a whole. While it can be sown nearly all year round, best results are achieved if you sow in the spring and early autumn. It can take most weather a British winter throws at it but would benefit from protection from snow and frost during the winter months, such as a cloche or horticultural fleece.  Sow February to March under cover, and then March to May and September. Harvest May to December if the winter is mild.","image":"sepa11717.jpg","commonName":"lettuce 'Marvel of Four Seasons'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":319168,"botanicalName":"<em>Lactuca</em> <em>sativa</em> 'Maureen'","entityDescription":"A compact, leafy biennial usually grown as an annual. This cos type lettuce produces uniform small, dense, heads with crisp, yellow hearts from spring to autumn according to sowing date","image":"","commonName":"lettuce (Cos) 'Maureen'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":517368,"botanicalName":"<em>Lactuca</em> <em>sativa</em> 'Miniko'","entityDescription":"A compact, leafy biennial usually grown as an annual. This sweet-tasting mini iceberg lettuce produces small lettuces which can be harvested one per meal in spring, summer or autumn, depending on the date of sowing.  Shows good resistance to bolting","image":"","commonName":null,"nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":208400,"botanicalName":"<em>Lactuca</