B0017564_13512.jpg","commonName":"aubergine 'Scorpio'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":65293,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>nigrum</em>","entityDescription":"A fast-growing annual or biennial with variable habit, often found in woodland or areas of disturbed soil. Leaves are broadly ovate, sometimes with wavy edges. Flowers are small, white and star-shaped, with five petals and prominent yellow anthers, and followed by clusters of round dark green berries that are matt black when ripe","image":"WSYD0016103.jpg","commonName":"black nightshade","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":66889,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>pseudocapsicum</em>","entityDescription":"A small, upright, bushy, evergreen shrub to 30cm, usually grown as a winter-fruiting annual. Leaves are narrow, dark green and glossy, with wavy-edges. In summer, it produces small clusters of white, star-shaped flowers, followed by long-lasting, spherical, red, yellow or orange fruit 1.5 to 2cm across","image":"visi94229.jpg","commonName":"Christmas cherry","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":{"plantId":66889,"price":"£6.99","oldPrice":null,"url":"https://www.rhsplants.co.uk/plants/_/solanum-pseudocapsicum/classid.2000050829/sku.RH30007523/"}},{"id":106242,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em>","entityDescription":"Potatoes are hugely versatile and a staple ingredient of many meals in one form or another – boiled, mashed, chipped or baked. Potatoes are classified as being either earlies or maincrops. Early varieties are ready to harvest much sooner than maincrops and are what we call ‘new potatoes’. Maincrop varieties are in the ground a lot longer and produce a larger harvest and bigger potatoes. There is a huge variety of cultivars to choose from.\r\n\r\nThe potato plant is a tuberous perennial grown as annual up to 60cm tall, with compound, green leaves and white, pink or purple, star-shaped flowers. The underground stems named stolons will form few to many tubers of different size and colour. The tuber bear small buds, from which all potaotes are vegetatively propagated","image":"sepa15642.jpg","commonName":"potato","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":517352,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Acoustic'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A high-yielding second early potato ready to lift in July/August, with waxy, pale yellow flesh, good for salads and for boiling.  If lifted later in the year, it becomes more floury and better for chips, mash, baking or roasting.  Said to have a very strong resistance to blight","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Acoustic'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":517370,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Alanis'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A high-yielding main crop potato with long, pale-yellow tubers with shallow 'eyes', ideal for chipping and roasting as tubers are large and floury.  Shows good heat and drought tolerance and stores well long-term","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Alanis'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":148631,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Anya'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers.  A second early potato with a slightly nutty flavour. The long, narrow tubers are ideal for steaming, boiling and roasting","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Anya'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":384055,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Arran Pilot'","entityDescription":"A first early variety of potato and traditional favourite due to its excellent taste and high yields. Potatoes are white-skinned with creamy-white flesh, delicious eaten as a new or salad potato straight out of the ground. Shows good resistance to scab.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Arran Pilot'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":165337,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Arran Victory'","entityDescription":"This maincrop, heritage potato was bred on the Isle of Arran to celebrate the end of the First World War. It is now quite rare but worth growing if you can find it as they are supposed to make the best roast potatoes! The potatoes are oval with purple-blue skin, which fades during cooking, and has bright white flesh with a floury texture. Also good to bake, steam, chip and mash. This variety can get quite tall so sheltered ground is best.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Arran Victory'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":298671,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Blue Danube'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A fast-growing, early maincrop potato ready to lift in the autumn, with purple-black stems, dark, glossy green foliage and pretty purple flowers.  The blue-skinned, white-fleshed, well-shaped tubers are perfect for roasting (some say 'the best roast potato ever').  Shows good resistance to blight and potato viruses","image":"potatoSarpoBlueDanube5.JPG","commonName":"potato 'Blue Danube'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133347,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'British Queen'","entityDescription":"This traditional second early, bred over 100 years ago in Scotland, is easy to grow and produces a uniform crop with good yields. The tubers are oval, white skinned with white flesh and have a floury texture and delicious flavour. Suitable for all cooking uses but cook with skins on to retain the flavour.","image":"potatoBritishQueen019.JPG","commonName":"potato 'British Queen'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":139335,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Cara'","entityDescription":"A high yielding maincrop which produces lots of uniform, rounded, pink and white tubers with a floury white flesh. The potatoes have a sweet taste and are a great all purpose variety which stores well. It also has excellent disease resistance and can tolerate drought conditions","image":"visi82591.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Cara'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":343452,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Carolus'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A maincrop variety that produces a good yield of attractive, uniformly oval tubers. The skin is yellow with small flushes of red and the flesh is light yellow in colour with a slightly floury texture when cooked and an excellent flavour. These potatoes are good for boiling, mashing, baking and roasting and as they have quite a high dry matter, they are also good for home frying. Excellent Potato blight and Potato rot resistance.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Carolus'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":301266,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Casablanca'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A new, multi-purpose first early potato with a smooth white skin, shallow eyes and a creamy flesh. It is an attractive potato, that is rapidly becoming the exhibitors favourite, while chefs are lapping it up because it is a dream to chip, bake or boil. Trials shows good resistance to Potato blackleg and it has been said that it can produce an edible crop just 62 days after planting.","image":"visi81811.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Casablanca'","nurseriesCount":8,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133348,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Charlotte'","entityDescription":"A popular second early salad variety which produces good yields of uniform potatoes.  Tubers are oval, have yellow, smooth skin with a creamy-yellow flesh and a waxy texture. They are delicious hot or cold. Some resistance to Potato blackleg","image":"potatoCharlotte0511.JPG","commonName":"potato 'Charlotte'","nurseriesCount":7,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149189,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Colleen'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A tender, upright, branching perennial first early variety with dark green foliage, purple flowers and short, oval tubers with white skin and some resistance to blight.  Good for all cooking methods and high yielding.  Available to harvest June to July","image":"visi72499.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Colleen'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":333783,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Desiree'","entityDescription":"This early maincrop potato has oval red-skinned tubers with pale yellow flesh that keeps a firm texture when cooked and store well once harvested. They are good all-rounders and are particularly good as a baking potato, making these firm favourites. They are heavy croppers that are tolerant of drought, and show a good resistance to Potato blight and some resistance to Potato scab.","image":"PotatoDesiree.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Desiree'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":{"plantId":333783,"price":"£8.99","oldPrice":null,"url":"https://www.rhsplants.co.uk/plants/_/potato-desiree/classid.2000002442/"}},{"id":199781,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Duke of York'","entityDescription":"A heritage potato bred in 1891. This potato is much valued for its pale yellow tubers that have a super rich flavour. A classic first early which is low growing so ideal for a windy garden. Perfect for new potatoes but can be left to develop into a quality general purpose potato.","image":"visi72479.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Duke of York'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":165338,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Edzell Blue'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A second early potato with bluish-purple skin and white flesh. The tubers are round and quite small. A floury potato, making it good for baking, frying and mashing","image":"visi72509.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Edzell Blue'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133344,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Foremost'","entityDescription":"Tender perennial with compact, upright green leaves, producing waxy white flesh tubers in summer. Has good resistance to slugs.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Foremost'","nurseriesCount":5,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149812,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Frieslander'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. An early potato with round to oval tubers, yellowish skin and pale, firm flesh. Suitable for boiling, baking and frying","image":"visi25421.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Frieslander'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149814,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Harmony'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"This early maincrop gives high yields of clean, white skinned potatoes that are resistant to scab and blackspot and are excellent to store. Popular as an exhibition variety and as a great baking potato.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Harmony'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":278381,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Highland Burgundy Red'","entityDescription":"This heritage variety is a unique looking maincrop potato that has red skin and red flesh with a white ring under the skin. It has a sweet taste and floury texture so is excellent for novelty roasties, crisps and chips and also good for steaming - they are best cooked with their skins on to retain their colour. Produces moderate yields with high numbers of tubers per plant.","image":"visi72425.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Highland Burgundy Red'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":307248,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Home Guard'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A first early potato that has remained popular since the 1940's. Oval tubers have pale skin with firm, creamy white flesh, suitable for boiling, baking, roasting, frying and mashing. An all-rounder with good flavour","image":"visi72493.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Home Guard'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":307249,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'International Kidney'","entityDescription":"First introduced in 1879, these potatoes are still sought after today for their sublime texture, thin skins and rich, buttery flavour. When grown on the island of Jersey these potatoes are better known as 'Jersey Royals'.  Traditionally known as an early maincrop, it is usually grown (and sold in the supermarkets) as a new, second early or salad potato. It's a first class all-rounder!","image":"visi82410.jpg","commonName":"potato 'International Kidney'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":318500,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Jazzy'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A modern second early variety which produces large quantities of small tubers. The potatoes are visually appealing with cream skin and light yellow flesh and have a nice waxy texture and good flavour - great for salads, boiled and roasted.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Jazzy'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149202,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Kestrel'","entityDescription":"A fairly recent introduction to the market which is fast becoming a household favourite due to its delicious flavour. This second early potato has smooth skin with attractive with purple blue tints in places and is a great all rounder in the kitchen. It is a high yielding variety which grows well in heavy soils and tolerates dry conditions. Shows good resistance to Potato blackleg, as well as potato virus, slugs and bruising.","image":"PotatoKestrel.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Kestrel'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":309096,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'King Edward'","entityDescription":"This maincrop potato was introduced in 1902 and has remained popular ever since due to its versatility and delicious taste. A firm favourite, which has creamy-white flesh that rarely discolours on cooking, it is perfect for roasting and general kitchen use. It produces a high number of tubers per plant and has good resistance to Potato scab, spraing, mild mosaic virus and slugs.","image":"visi82660.jpg","commonName":"potato 'King Edward'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133351,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Lady Christl'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"Perennial of branching stems with compound leaves, white flowers and green berries that forms swollen, waxy, edible tubers harvested in summer. Second early potato with pale yellow skin, firm flesh and fantastic flavour. Good eelworm resistance.","image":"PUB0031482.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Lady Christl'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":148735,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Laura'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. An early potato with red skin and yellow flesh. High yields of large, oval-shaped tubers","image":"grjo02173.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Laura'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149825,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Marfona'","entityDescription":"A popular second early potato due to consistently producing high yields of smooth jacket-sized potatoes. Tubers are firm and waxy with yellow skin and creamy flesh. Popular in the supermarkets as an early jacket potato and shows good resistance to Potato rot.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Marfona'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149827,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Maris Bard'","entityDescription":"A heavy cropping, first early potato that is ready to lift early in the season and produces delicious white skinned and white fleshed tubers. Hailed as one of the best and most reliable, its semi-dry flesh makes it ideal for frying, or boiling as a salad potato. Shows good resistance to drought, damage and bruising.","image":"visi72431.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Maris Bard'","nurseriesCount":6,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":287322,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Maris Peer'","entityDescription":"A second early, with uniform, smaller than average potatoes and a good yield. Flavour is subtle but delicious and ideal for boiling, steaming or roasting whole. They have a light skin, creamy firm flesh which doesn’t disintegrate during cooking. Shows good resistance to Potato scab, bruising, splitting and skin spot. Some growers recommend as a great variety to plant in August and crop from late October to mid-December.","image":"visi82407.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Maris Peer'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":309097,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Maris Piper'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. This is a reliable maincrop potato, with heavy crops of oval tubers, with cream-coloured skin and flesh and good flavour","image":"visi81773.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Maris Piper'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":148617,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Markies'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A recently introduced maincrop variety which has good yields and makes great chips! Viewed as a good all rounder in the kitchen, the oval tubers have cream skin and a slightly yellow flesh. This cultivar shows a high tolerance to drought and good general disease resistance.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Markies'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":112464,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Maxine'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"This early maincrop variety produces high yields of uniform red skinned tubers with white waxy flesh. It keeps quite well and is good for baking, boiling and roasting although the taste has been described as nondescript. It shows resistance to drought, Potato blackleg, powdery scab and and some Potato cyst nematodes.","image":"PotatoMaxine.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Maxine'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":292608,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Michelle'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A maincrop potato with smooth, pale skin and waxy, yellow flesh. High-yielding and stores well","image":"zidi00095.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Michelle'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":229377,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Mozart'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A maincrop potato. Large, oval-shaped tubers have red skin and pale yellow flesh","image":"visi82561.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Mozart'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133352,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Nadine'","entityDescription":"A second early that produces a high yield of attractive and uniform tubers. It’s firm flesh has a slightly sweet taste and is ideal for baking but is also suitable for boiling and chipping. The tubers are smooth, white skinned with cream coloured flesh and show some resistance to Potato cyst nematodes and scab.","image":"PotatoNadine.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Nadine'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":199924,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Nicola'","entityDescription":"The smooth oval tubers of this second early look good and are one of the tastiest salad potatoes. They have a firm waxy texture and are great for boiling or sautéing. Easy to grow in pots, bags or borders, they produce a generous number of tubers per plant, and as they store well, you will usually be able to enjoy them over a couple of months. Shows resistance to potato leafroll virus and some potato cyst nematodes.","image":"visi74428.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Nicola'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":148731,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Orla'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A first early, which can be left to bulk up as a second early or even maincrop, with a great taste that's best suited to boiling. Skins are thin and light brown, getting tougher the longer it's in the ground and the flesh is yellow and slightly waxy, although again, if left in the ground it increases in size and becomes more floury. Shows excellent resistance to potato virus, late Potato blight on tubers and bruising and can tolerate drought.","image":"visi72428.jpg","commonName":"potato (early) 'Orla'","nurseriesCount":5,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":304422,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Pentland Javelin'","entityDescription":"This is first early potato takes a week or two longer than other cultivars to bulk up but then produces a high number of tubers per plant. It can also be left in the ground longer which results in a larger, more floury potato. It is a firm favourite with creamy-white flesh that rarely discolours on cooking and is best boiled as a salad or new potato.  It has good resistance to Potato scab, mild mosaic virus, slugs and bruising.","image":"visi72481.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Pentland Javelin'","nurseriesCount":5,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":112466,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Picasso'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A high-yielding early maincrop potato variety with pale, golden skin and red eyes. Good disease and drought resistance","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Picasso'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":292610,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Piccolo Star'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A second early potato with yellowish skin and pale, waxy flesh. Small, uniform tubers are ideal for boiling and steaming","image":"visi81801.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Piccolo Star'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":139340,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Ratte'","entityDescription":"A second early to main variety that has been popular in France for over 70 years due to its delicious tubers with a distinctive chestnut flavour. The tubers are long, oval-shaped and have smooth skin with waxy yellow flesh. They don't disintegrate during cooking and are delicious steamed, boiled and as a salad potato. The yields produced are moderate, not as productive as other varieties,  but is worth the smaller number of tubers for the excellent taste.","image":"","commonName":"potato (salad) 'Ratte'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133345,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Red Duke of York'","entityDescription":"A heritage first early potato bred in 1942 with an excellent flavour. It is a good all rounder but particularly good boiled or as a salad potato. The deep red skin and pale, yellow, floury flesh make it an attractive variety to grow. It is generally preferred to the original Duke of York variety due to it being more vigorous, having larger tubers and a better taste. It has quite low disease resistance but its taste and looks still make it a popular variety.","image":"potatoRedDuke119.JPG","commonName":"potato 'Red Duke of York'","nurseriesCount":6,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":139344,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Rocket'","entityDescription":"One of the earliest of the first earlies, this is a heavy cropper and produces attractive, evenly sized potatoes. They have white waxy flesh which remains firm on cooking, not the most memorable flavour but best boiled or steamed. They are not great in storage so be aware of this when planting. Shows resistance to some Potato cyst nematode.","image":"potatoRocket.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Rocket'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149190,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Rooster'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"This maincrop is hugely popular due to its beautiful taste, good yields and versatility. It is easily recognisable by its red skin and creamy yellow flesh and makes excellent chips, mash, roasties and jacket potatoes! Shows some resistance to Potato blackleg and potato leafroll virus.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Rooster'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":505701,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Sarpo Blue Danube'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A fast-growing, early maincrop potato ready to lift in the autumn, with purple-black stems, dark, glossy green foliage and pretty purple flowers.  The blue-skinned, white-fleshed, well-shaped tubers are perfect for roasting (some say 'the best roast potato ever').  Shows good resistance to blight and potato viruses","image":"potatoSarpoBlueDanube5.JPG","commonName":"potato 'Blue Danube'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":298671,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Blue Danube'","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":198017,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Sarpo Mira'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A high-yielding, red-skinned late maincrop variety that produces a good amount of weed-smothering foliage, but it is the potatoes natural resistance to blight that makes it stand out from the crowd. It is a good all rounder in the kitchen and has a floury texture that is great for baking, roasting and making chips. It also has good crop yields and stores well so the good harvest potential will mean you do not have to eat them all at once. Also shows good resistance to Potato blackleg, slugs and some potato viruses.","image":"PotatoSarpoMira.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Sarpo Mira'","nurseriesCount":6,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149186,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Saxon'","entityDescription":"This second early cultivar is high yielding, has a lovely flavour and maintains a good texture when boiled or baked. The tubers are attractive, oval-shaped with white skin and cream flesh and suitable for all kitchen uses. Good disease resistance and the ability to store long term make this potato a great all rounder.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Saxon'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":199780,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Sharpe's Express'","entityDescription":"An heirloom first early variety introduced in 1900 and was apparently Percy Thrower’s favourite. It is slightly pear shaped with bright white flesh, smooth skin and a superb 'new potato' flavour. Best boiled or steamed whole in skins it is great hot with butter or cold in salads and it’s floury texture also means it makes a great roastie!","image":"visi72490.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Sharpe's Express'","nurseriesCount":3,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149854,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Stemster'","entityDescription":"A bushy perennial grown as an annual vegetable for its edible tubers. A high-yielding maincrop potato with pinkish-red skin and pale yellow flesh. Tubers are large and store well. A good choice for drier soils and suitable for boiling, mashing, baking and roasting","image":"zidi01539.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Stemster'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":220712,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Sunrise'","entityDescription":"A maincrop potato with good drought tolerance producing white-skinned, light yellow-fleshed tubers that store well over winter","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Sunrise'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":139346,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Swift'","entityDescription":"Hailed as one of the earliest croppers, it is claimed that you can be dishing these potatoes up in as little as 7 weeks after you plant them (10 weeks might be more realistic). These first earlies produce a high yield of white-skinned, oval potatoes that have a creamy coloured flesh that is ideal for boiling. In growth, they are compact, which makes them ideal for containers and less sheltered ground. They show a good resistance to bruising, Potato scab and virus.","image":"grjo02184.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Swift'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":229642,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Vales Sovereign'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A maincrop potato bred by the Scottish Crop Research Institute and introduced after extensive trials. It has a classic large, oval shape, with red blushes to the pale skin and creamy flesh, a velvety texture, and works well in all general kitchen use. It is resistant to diseases, doesn't bruise easily, with a consistant high yield regardless of weather conditions","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Vales Sovereign'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":148558,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Vivaldi'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"An easy to grow and high-yielding variety that may be lifted for baby potatoes or left in the ground longer for larger, early maincrop potatoes. Pale golden tubers are good boiled, baked, mashed or roasted. Can be grown in containers","image":"","commonName":"potato (early) 'Vivaldi'","nurseriesCount":4,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":149864,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Wilja'","entityDescription":"This second early potato is noted for its tasty tubers, which have a medium-dry texture, making it a great all rounder. The long oval yellow tubers have creamy yellow flesh which holds its shape well (even if it's been boiled for a little too long), and as the tubers tend to keep well, they can be enjoyed over a long period. Shows good resistance to Potato rot, Potato scab and potato leafroll virus.","image":"","commonName":"potato 'Wilja'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":133346,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> 'Winston'","entityDescription":"Forming handsome, good sized tubers, which have a smooth skin and a creamy white flesh, these fast-growing potatoes are ready to harvest early in the season. This is a sought after variety if you are growing for the shows, and it also has a good resistance to drought, heat, potato viruses and bruising.","image":"RHS_WSY0010531_12042.JPG","commonName":"potato 'Winston'","nurseriesCount":2,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":true,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":230999,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> (Phureja Group) 'Mayan Gold'<sup>PBR</sup>","entityDescription":"A tender, upright, branching perennial maincrop variety with dark green foliage, purple flowers and long, oval tubers with golden yellow skin and a nutty flavour.  Good for most cooking methods except boiling when they tend to fall apart.  Available to harvest June to August","image":"visi82663.jpg","commonName":"potato 'Mayan Gold'","nurseriesCount":1,"synonymParentPlantId":0,"synonymParentPlantName":null,"isAgm":false,"isSynonym":false,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":null},{"id":337023,"botanicalName":"<em>Solanum</em> <em>tuberosum</em> var. <em>vulgare</em>","entityDescription":"Potatoes are hugely versatile and a staple ingredient of many meals in one form or another – boiled, mashed, chipped or baked. Potatoes are classified as being either earlies or maincrops. Early varieties are ready to h